---
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-CA">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <SEO
      title="Editorial Policy"
      description="How SmallSpace Home researches, writes, tests, and updates content — our sourcing standards, correction policy, and independence from brands."
      path="/editorial-policy"
      type="website"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-N5MCBQG6"
    height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript>
    <Header />

    <main class="policy-page">
      <section class="policy-hero">
        <div class="policy-hero-inner">
          <span class="section-eyebrow">How We Work</span>
          <h1 class="policy-heading">Editorial Policy</h1>
          <p class="policy-sub">How we research, write, test, and correct what we publish.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-body">
        <div class="policy-inner">

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Who writes this</h2>
            <p>
              SmallSpace Home is written and maintained by Badreddine Br, a renter living in a 510 sq ft
              Toronto apartment. This is not a large editorial team — it's one person testing real
              products and layouts in a real rental, then writing up what actually worked and what
              didn't. See the <a href="/about">About page</a> for the full story.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>How we research and write</h2>
            <p>
              Every guide starts from a real constraint — a small kitchen, a rented living room, a
              closet with no organizer system — and works through solutions we've either tried
              ourselves or researched carefully from Canadian retailers (IKEA Canada, Amazon.ca,
              HomeSense, Wayfair Canada, Canadian Tire, Structube) so prices and availability are
              accurate for a Canadian audience, not adapted from US content.
            </p>
            <p>
              We use AI-assisted tools to help with research, drafting, and editing efficiency. Every
              piece of advice, every price, and every product recommendation is reviewed by a human
              before publishing — nothing goes live unchecked.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Product recommendations</h2>
            <p>
              We recommend specific products (often IKEA or Amazon.ca items) because they're genuinely
              useful for small Canadian apartments, not because of a paid placement. If a post ever
              contains a sponsored product or affiliate link, it will be clearly disclosed at the top
              of that article. As of now, this site does not run affiliate links or sponsored content.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
            <p>
              Prices, retailer stock, and product availability change. If you spot something outdated
              or incorrect, <a href="/contact">let us know</a> — we update posts when we confirm an
              error, and note significant changes in the post's "last updated" date rather than
              silently editing published claims.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <h2>What we don't do</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>We don't publish staged, unrealistic "after" photos we haven't actually recreated in a real small space.</li>
              <li>We don't inflate prices or omit cheaper alternatives to make a paid product look better.</li>
              <li>We don't accept payment in exchange for a positive review.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-block">
            <p class="policy-contact-line">
              Questions about how a specific post was researched or written? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> — we're happy to explain.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.policy-page { padding-bottom: 0; }

.policy-hero {
  background: var(--color-ink);
  padding: 96px 24px 64px;
}
.policy-hero-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.section-eyebrow {
  font-size: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-accent);
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.policy-heading {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
  font-weight: 400;
  color: #fff;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
  line-height: 1.1;
}
.policy-sub {
  font-size: 1rem;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);
  margin: 0;
}

.policy-body {
  background: var(--color-white);
  padding: 72px 24px 96px;
}
.policy-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.policy-block { margin-bottom: 44px; }
.policy-block:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.policy-block h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--color-ink);
  margin: 0 0 16px;
}
.policy-block p {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
}
.policy-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.policy-block a { color: var(--color-accent-dark); }
.policy-block ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 1.3rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
.policy-block ul li {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
.policy-contact-line {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 1.05rem !important;
  color: var(--color-accent-dark) !important;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .policy-hero { padding: 64px 20px 48px; }
  .policy-body { padding: 48px 20px 64px; }
}
</style>
